<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine Senate ratifies membership in sugar body.</title>
<headline>Philippine Senate ratifies membership in sugar body.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Senate ratified on Monday the 1992 International Sugar Agreement, paving the way for its reentry to the International Sugar Organization (ISO).</p>
<p>Senate ratification is required to make an international agreement valid.</p>
<p>The Philippines was a signatory to previous international sugar accords but it withdrew from the ISO in 1991 due to disagreements on the amount of yearly membership dues.</p>
<p>The 1992 Agreement reduced the amount of Philippine contribution to the ISO budget.</p>
